#: ../../../src/python/_autosummary/mlx.core.unique.rst:2
msgid "mlx.core.unique"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:1
msgid "Returns the sorted unique elements of the flattened array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:3
msgid ""
"The shape of the output does not depend on the values in ``a``, so ``a`` is "
"not evaluated. Unlike NumPy, the size is never inferred from the values and "
"must be provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:7
msgid ""
"Entries past the last unique element hold ``fill_value`` and their count is "
"``0``, so ``mx.sum(counts > 0)`` gives the number of unique elements as long "
"as the output is not truncated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:11
msgid ""
"A truncated output keeps the smallest ``size`` unique elements, and "
"``index``, ``inverse`` and ``counts`` then stop describing all of ``a``, and "
"``inverse`` and ``counts`` stop agreeing with each other: the counts of the "
"dropped elements are gone, while their indices in ``inverse`` are clamped to "
"the last entry. ``inverse`` is meaningless for a ``size`` of ``0``, since "
"there is no element left for it to point at."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:19
msgid ""
"This op builds on ``mx.sort``, so a ``bool`` input needs the CPU stream, "
"which is where ``mx.sort`` supports it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:22
msgid "Input array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:24
msgid ""
"The size of the output. If the size is smaller than the number of unique "
"elements of ``a``, the output is truncated. If it is larger, the output is "
"padded with ``fill_value``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:28
msgid ""
"If ``True``, also return the index in the flattened ``a`` of the first "
"occurrence of each unique element. Default: ``False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:32
msgid ""
"If ``True``, also return the indices of the unique array that rebuild ``a``. "
"The indices have the same shape as ``a``. Default: ``False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:36
msgid ""
"If ``True``, also return the number of times each unique element occurs in "
"``a``. Default: ``False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:39
msgid ""
"The value of the entries past the last unique element. If ``None``, this "
"defaults to the first of the sorted unique elements. Default: ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:0
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:44
msgid ""
"The sorted unique elements. If any of ``return_index``, ``return_inverse`` "
"or ``return_counts`` is ``True``, a tuple with the requested arrays in the "
"order values, index, inverse, counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../docstring of mlx.core.unique:0
msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

